From: fxtec-pro1x-guix
Subject: [PATCH] json_object_put: free containers also when NDEBUG is set

json_object_put frees each container's memory in
assert(_json_object_put_maybe_free(jso, 1) == 0).  With NDEBUG (release
builds), assert does not evaluate its argument, so every JSON object and
array that held children was never freed: every parse leaked.  Seen in
swaybar, which leaked about 0.5 GB an hour on a phone (one status line a
second), and in a loop of json_tokener_parse + json_object_put.  Call it
outside the assert.
---
--- a/json_object.c
+++ b/json_object.c
@@ -439,7 +439,9 @@
 			// so we need to actually free it now
 			assert(jso->_ref_count == 0);
 			jso->_ref_count++;   // We're the exclusive owner of jso, non-atomic add is ok.
-			assert(_json_object_put_maybe_free(jso, 1) == 0);
+			int freed = _json_object_put_maybe_free(jso, 1);
+			assert(freed == 0);
+			(void)freed;
 			jso = parent;
 			// iteration will be reset at the top of the loop
 		}
